<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Train O1 ~ one face's sessions

!! Contents

* [[Ground and crew|#/ground]] · [[Commit walk|#/walk]] · [[Witness and red window|#/witness]] · [[Collision sheet|#/collisions]] · [[Done when|#/done]] · [[Rulings|#/rulings]].

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/ground`>>

!! Ground and crew

Start the live session callers after W hands over verified face sessions and its vessel composers. One compose lead owns node and browser mount sites. Narrow builders own working-address derivation, receipts and the control leg. The lead alone moves both callers through the scoped view. The session contract, `session-document-view.ts`, `resolveSurfaceRecipe` and `mountSurface` already supply the pure seam.

The working address derives from three inputs: a verified face secret scoped to its Nexus, the canonical wiki relation, and the slot kind. O1's lead fixes the exact input encoding, domain label, key treatment and output address before a module or caller mints any byte. Two offline vessels holding the same face secret and relation converge; another face, relation or slot diverges. The address reveals neither the face secret nor a roster. An unavailable face secret refuses attach. This contract waits on identity material from N and W; no stand-alone `working-address.ts` lands ahead of that choice.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/walk`>>

!! Commit walk

# ''PURE: address and receipt vectors.'' Fix the working-address image with N's identity lead, then derive offline convergence and separation vectors. Define a durability receipt on the authenticated session carrying `docUrl`, the stored heads and the holder's boot epoch; send it only after the holder commits those heads, with no clock in the frame. Keep receipt truth behind the vessel owner's storage acknowledgement.
# ''LIVE: scoped surface mounts.'' Open the verified session, resolve its recipe once, construct its face facets and call `mountSurface` from node and browser production sites. The share verdict guards the offered facet list. The leaf and hearth each wear their one-way canon gate. A catalog ask and a content read cross the same view as document fetch, write and announce.
# ''LIVE: hands and controls.'' Move node verbs, watcher, seat, effect index and outcome reader to session scope. Give the browser holder unicast replies and one control-event leg for keys, files, drops, Escape, Ctrl-Enter and import. Bind parallel-draft attribution to the authenticated session face.
# ''LIVE: switch and fleet.'' Switch one tab's session without ending another. Retire the vessel-wide selector and the last `mountWiki` production caller. Expose the person's fleet view and removal through the verified session door.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/witness`>>

!! Witness and red window

The working address takes a behavioural witness, never a declared red that pins an export name: open the same face secret, wiki relation and slot on two independent offline vessels and expect one address; vary each input alone and expect a different one; refuse an attach without the secret. Unskip `PRODUCTION_SURFACES_USE_SCOPED_VIEW` when both callers mount surfaces. Keep the broad-port red until the last interactive `mountWiki` path leaves. Prove that two faces cannot fetch each other's document or catalog name, two offline vessels derive one working address, restart reads a persisted receipt, and one tab's switch leaves the second tab live. A failed attach refuses boot visibly.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/collisions`>>

!! Collision sheet

| Seam | O1 hand-off |
|---|---|
| N | Consume final face identity and joint AID; leave charter and inception bytes with N. |
| W | Take `open-node-vessel.ts` and `open-browser-vessel.ts` session hunks after W's socket cutover; leave W's wire and gate proof intact. |
| S8 | Consume sealed selves rows; leave `persona-selves-plane.ts` and `sealed-acts.ts` with S8. |
| Sealed-store step 3 | Hand over verified face, signer and scoped fetch path before storage hydration changes. |
| H and X | H consumes the worn face's hosting authority through its own delegation. X consumes O1's live browser and node legs; neither edits O1's address bytes. |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/done`>>

!! Done when

Every interactive node and browser surface mounts under a verified face and scoped view. One address follows each face, wiki relation and slot kind. Receipts survive restart. Two tabs hold independent sessions; controls, verbs, drafts, fleet removal and catalog reads follow the face. No enabled production caller opens a broad wiki port.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/rulings`>>

!! Rulings

The working address's input contract stands ruled (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/rulings`>>, the working address): O1's pure step builds its vectors to those bytes, and the fleet-join door of train W delivers the face address secret.

The roadmap's ONE FACE path and `F1`–`F12` name the session debt (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-loops`>>; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-road`>>). Its standing law keeps the face at the session capability (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/decisions`>>). O1 fixes no address bytes before the identity input contract lands. A change to that contract needs an explicit identity ruling.

<<~/ahu>>

